{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftKS5dQrwtazypC5FAeJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Yes, build it and run it as the randomized test.** It costs three days, the downside is small, and the test answers the question the survey can't.\n\n**Why the survey alone isn't enough:**\n- **Response bias.** 38% is a share of the 61% who answered. Non-responders may leave for other reasons, such as price or food quality. The real share wanting a break could be anywhere from about 23% (if no non-responder does) up to 38% or more.\n- **Survey answers aren't behaviour.** \"Travelling\" is an easy, polite reason to give. Some of these people would never have come back anyway.\n- **Cannibalization.** Seasonal cancellers may already come back on their own. If they do, a pause only changes how they return, not whether they return. You need your current reactivation rate as the baseline.\n\n**How to judge the test:**\n- **Main metric:** revenue or active subscribers per person who reaches the cancel page, measured 90–180 days later and compared across both arms. Don't use \"pauses taken\"; it will look good regardless.\n- **Watch for:** pauses that end in a cancellation, complaints or chargebacks when billing restarts, and support tickets.\n- **Sample size:** about 3,900 cancellers a quarter gives roughly 1,950 per arm. That can detect a retention lift of several percentage points, but not a small one. Plan for at least one quarter, and remember travel season affects how many people want a pause.\n\n**Build details that matter:**\n- Send a clear reminder before billing restarts. Auto-renewal laws in many places require one, and it protects trust.\n- Make skipping the pause and cancelling one click. If the pause feels like an obstacle, it will hurt how people see you and may create legal risk.\n- Log the pause length people choose. That tells you whether 1–8 weeks is the right range.\n\n**Decision rule:** keep the pause if retained revenue is meaningfully higher in the pause arm and complaints don't rise."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3194,"cache_read_input_tokens":5018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3194},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6b0a5f3f-fb5a-4fff-a398-b179f661563d","uuid":"3acc5f03-121d-4457-8c31-203e24864f13","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:27:39.185Z","request_id":"req_011CftKS5QXXbgQBAkvnBsRw"}
